      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T05:51:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The biggest difference between the NVIDIA and AMD implementations is the MCTP message type. AMD uses 0x7F (Vendor Defined - IANA), while NVIDIA uses 0x7E, resulting in a different message format.\n\nRegarding the MCTP transport layer, we discussed this with @patrick@stwcx.xyz and @pmb@meta.com earlier [1]. We plan to implement the MCTP request/response layer using sdbusplus::async [2] instead of the Boost-based library. The nvidia-gpusensor implementation can migrate to the new library once it is available.\n\n[1] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/94550/comment/10c40fe3_baa69d09/\n[2] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/95106",
